From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:55:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ui/dbus: give a console without GL the 2D listener

With GL on, every D-Bus listener gets the GL operations, but the D-Bus
display gives a GL context only to graphic consoles. A text console, as
for a serial port or the monitor shown in a "vc", has none, and so its
surface has no texture: a client that listens to it has
dbus_scanout_texture() called with texture 0, and on a host with GBM
QEMU aborts on its assert(tex_id).

Choose the listener's operations by whether its console has a GL
context.

Fixes: 142ca628a733 ("ui: add a D-Bus display backend")
Cc: qemu-stable@nongnu.org
Signed-off-by: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 ui/dbus-listener.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ui/dbus-listener.c b/ui/dbus-listener.c
index 7143c3e6ea..d594606656 100644
--- a/ui/dbus-listener.c
+++ b/ui/dbus-listener.c
@@ -1302,7 +1302,11 @@ dbus_display_listener_new(const char *bus_name,
     con = qemu_console_lookup_by_index(dbus_display_console_get_index(console));
     assert(con);
 #ifdef CONFIG_OPENGL
-    if (display_opengl) {
+    /*
+     * A console without a GL context, as a text console, has surfaces
+     * without a texture: its listeners get the 2D operations.
+     */
+    if (display_opengl && qemu_console_has_gl(con)) {
         ops = &dbus_gl_dcl_ops;
     }
 #endif
